# Conformance probe pack for the mapping rules of spec 0.6 on the `json` wire.
# Public. No kinds. Exercises `const` (string, number, boolean, forced string),
# `default`, value tables with `via` (wire int to model string, wire string to
# model int, and same-type pass-through), one key at two locators, and `typemap`
# on a wire other than xml and geojson (ruling 18 of 0.5).
format  conformance-rules-json
version 0.6.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses    track
wire    json
const   schema           rules
field   uid              id            string
const   rev              6                        # written as the number 6
field   type             kind          string     # through the pack-wide typemap
field   lat              pos.lat       float
field   lat              pos.latitude  float      # the same key at a second locator
field   lon              pos.lon       float
field   hae              pos.alt       float
field   track.class      cls           int     via class    # wire integer, model string
field   how              how           string  via how      # both sides string: a value with no entry passes through
field   track.confirmed  status        string  via status   # wire string, model int
const   meta.live        true                     # written as the boolean true
const   meta.tag         =7                       # written as the string "7"
default hae              -1
default track.class      bird                     # the default goes through the table: written as 2
typemap F  a-f-G
map     class   1    uas
map     class   2    bird
map     class   3    uas                          # shares its model value with the first entry: encode writes 1
map     class   1    balloon                      # shares its wire value with the first entry: decode reads uas
map     how     M    m-g
map     status  yes  1
map     status  no   0
